    * for tiber_read(int fd, ...) or tiber_write(int fd, ...) or even tiber_connect and tiber_accept
      * in a loop first attempt to call it optimistically, if it fails with EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK/EINPROGRESS go ahead with the next part (always do the optimistic version first)
      * take lock
      * attempt to do non-blocking read or write again using the actual system call again just like the optimistic version, if success return with bytes written
      * if it fails with EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK/EINPROGRESS, then wait over read_wait or write_wait or read_or_write_wait
      * once woken up, release lock and continue
    * epoll loop is simple waits for N events, once received, based on the event takes lock and wakes up corresponding waiters
